        "content": "Web search results for query: \"\"shutup-mcp\" MCP proxy token reduction\"\n\nI'll search for information about \"shutup-mcp\" MCP proxy token reduction for you.**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"shutup-mcp MCP proxy token reduction\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"shutup-mcp - Zero-config MCP proxy that hides 99% of tools\", \"link\": \"https://www.hunted.space/product/shutup-mcp\", \"content\": \"Token reduction in my testing is ~98%—similar to what Redis and Atlassian reported with comparable approaches. It's v0.1.0, so there's plenty ...\", \"r...\n                                                ## Search Results: shutup-mcp MCP Proxy Token Reduction\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about **shutup-mcp** and its approach to MCP proxy token reduction:\n\n### Key Information\n\n**shutup-mcp** is a zero-configuration MCP (Model Context Protocol) proxy that significantly reduces token consumption by hiding tools from AI agents until they're actually needed.\n\n### Main Highlights:\n\n1. **Token Reduction Performance**\n   - Achieves approximately **98% token reduction** in testing\n   - Hides 99% of tools from agents initially, showing only what's needed\n\n2. **Key Features**\n   - Zero-config setup\n   - Shows agents only the tools they actually need\n   - No API keys required\n   - Similar results reported by Redis and Atlassian with comparable approaches\n\n3. **Benefits**\n   - **8x faster** performance\n   - **2x accuracy** improvement\n   - Reduces context clutter and latency\n\n### Relevant Links Found:\n\n- [shutup-mcp on Hunted Space](https://www.hunted.space/product/shutup-mcp) - Official product page\n- [shutup-mcp on Product Hunt](https://www.producthunt.com/products/shutup-mcp) - Product listing\n- [\"My AI Agent Could See 167 Tools. Then I Told It to shutup.\"](https://dev.to/hjs-foundation/my-ai-agent-could-see-167-tools-then-i-told-it-to-shutup-1kp9) - Technical article\n- [GitHub Repository](https://github.com/hjs-spec/shutup-mcp) - Source code (implied from results)\n\n### Context\n\nThe tool addresses the MCP token bloat problem where having many tools results in large tool definitions being loaded into the model context, making agents slower and more expensive to run. shutup-mcp solves this by only exposing relevant tools when needed rather than sending all tool definitions upfront.\n\nThe project is currently at version **v0.1.0**, indicating it's in early stages of development.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
